# Byte-exact test fixtures and the frozen migration-contract snapshot must
# never be rewritten by git's line-ending normalization, regardless of a
# contributor's or CI runner's core.autocrlf setting. Some golden inputs
# intentionally contain raw CR/CRLF bytes (they exist to exercise
# kernel/canonical.py's own LF normalization, per docs/mvp-spec.md §4.3); a
# plain `core.autocrlf=true` Windows checkout (the common Windows git default,
# also GitHub-hosted windows-latest runners' default) otherwise CRLF-mangles
# both those inputs and every canonical LF-only expected/snapshot file on
# checkout, causing spurious byte-exact test failures unrelated to any code
# defect.
tests/golden/** -text
docs/api-snapshot/openapi.json -text
